- Added Google conditional access settings (Fleet Premium): admins can connect Fleet to Google with the Google customer ID, the admin email and the customer's service account key, through the new `POST /api/v1/fleet/conditional_access/google` endpoint or `integrations.google_conditional_access` in `PATCH /api/v1/fleet/config` and GitOps (`customer_id`, `admin_email`, `api_key_json`). Fleet checks the domain-wide delegation with Google and stores the key encrypted; the key is always returned masked. `GET` returns the connection status and `DELETE` removes the integration. Removing the setting from GitOps YAML turns the integration off.
- Added a Google card to Settings > Integrations > Conditional access (Fleet Premium) to connect, edit and delete the Google conditional access integration. When the integration isn't connected, the card shows why.
